The type of guess in this code would have to be an integer and a string, and Rust requires that
guess have only one type. So what does continue return? How were we allowed to return a
u32 from one arm and have another arm that ends with continue in Listing 20-27?
As you might have guessed, continue has a ! value. That is, when Rust computes the type of
guess , it looks at both match arms, the former with a value of u32 and the latter with a !
value. Because ! can never have a value, Rust decides that the type of guess is u32 .
The formal way of describing this behavior is that expressions of type ! can be coerced into
any other type. We’re allowed to end this match arm with continue because continue
doesn’t return a value; instead, it moves control back to the top of the loop, so in the Err case,
we never assign a value to guess .
